# Paired with `web/Dockerfile`. Docker and podman both read the `.dockerignore` beside
# the Dockerfile when the build context is this directory.
#
# `node_modules` FIRST AND IT MATTERS MOST. The builder runs `npm ci` itself, so copying
# a host `node_modules` in would be slower AND wrong: this host is arm64 darwin and the
# image is arm64 linux, so any native binary in there is built for the wrong platform and
# fails at runtime with a message about an invalid ELF header rather than about the copy.
node_modules
.next
.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
